1. Aim :-
To study Microsoft Word and understand its features and applications.

2. Introduction :-
Microsoft Word is a word-processing application developed by Microsoft. 
It is used to create, edit, format, save and print documents.
It is widely used in schools, colleges, offices and businesses.

3. Features of MS Word :-
 - Text Editing: Allows users to create and edit text.
 - Text Formatting: Provides options to change font, size, colour and style.
 - Spell Check: Identifies spelling and grammatical mistakes.
 - Find and Replace: Helps find specific words and replace them.
 - Insert Tables: Allows users to create tables.
 - Insert Pictures: Allows users to add images and graphics.
 - Page Layout: Provides options for margins, orientation and page size.
 - Mail Merge: Helps create multiple personalized documents.
 - Header and Footer: Allows users to add information at the top and bottom of pages.
 - Printing: Allows users to print documents.

4. Components of MS Word Window :-
 Title Bar
 Quick Access Toolbar
 File Tab
  Ribbon
 Tabs
 Document Area
 Ruler
 Status Bar
 Scroll Bar
 Zoom Slider

5. Uses of MS Word :-
 - Creating letters and applications.
 - Preparing reports and assignments.
 - Making resumes and biodata.
 - Creating question papers.
 - Preparing official documents.

6. Advantages of MS Word :-
 - Easy to use.
 - Saves time and effort.
 - Provides professional formatting.
 - Allows easy editing.
 - Supports images, tables and charts.

7. Conclusion :-
Microsoft Word is an important word-processing application that makes
creating, editing and formatting documents easy and efficient.
